{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he was the son of an Egyptian man.</b> And so he had the audacity to bless [i.e., curse] the Name, for Israelites are not altogether coarse/wanting in shame."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase לָא פְקִירֵי כּוּלֵּי הָאִי literally means 'not entirely reckless/shameless'; Sforno uses it to explain why a full Israelite would not have behaved so brazenly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:42.887055882Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}